From: Mario Geiger <geiger.mario@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] P2P: CONNECTDONE does not overtake a relayed service's output

A git fetch from a P2P remote sometimes hangs forever after the last ACK:
GIT_TRACE_PACKET shows the final ACK and then no pack data. It happens in
about 2 of 100 fetches in a loop.

In runRelayService (P2P/IO.hs, line 398), relayReader, which reads the
output of upload-pack or receive-pack, and waitexit (line 436), which waits
for the process to exit, both put into one MVar RelayData. The process can
exit while relayReader still holds its last chunk; when RelayDone wins the
race for the MVar, relayHelper (line 450) sends CONNECTDONE and returns, and
the rest of the output is never sent. The client then waits forever for the
end of the pack. Because remotedaemon fetches inside its notification loop
(RemoteDaemon/Transport/P2PGeneric.hs), one hung fetch also stops every
later change notification from that peer.

Also, relayHelper sends CONNECTDONE when it takes RelayDone, and runrelay
(line 431) then sent a second CONNECTDONE.

Put RelayDone only after relayReader has reached EOF on the process's
output, and after the process has exited, from one thread; and send
CONNECTDONE once. A process that exits while a child of it still holds its
stdout open is now waited on until that child closes it.

Reproducer: lab/git-annex/ga-e25-relay-stress.py in
https://github.com/mariogeiger/pigeon (branch v2), which loops git fetch over
P2P with a new commit on each iteration.
---
 P2P/IO.hs | 23 ++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

--- a/P2P/IO.hs
+++ b/P2P/IO.hs
@@ -418,22 +418,27 @@
 	go (Just hin) (Just hout) _ pid = do
 		v <- newEmptyMVar
 		r <- withAsync (relayFeeder runner v hin) $ \_ ->
-			withAsync (relayReader v hout) $ \_ ->
-				withAsync (waitexit v pid) $ \_ -> do
-					r <- runrelay v
-					hClose hin
-					hClose hout
-					return r
+			withAsync (readthenwaitexit v hout pid) $ \_ -> do
+				r <- runrelay v
+				hClose hin
+				hClose hout
+				return r
 		void $ waitForProcess pid
 		return r
 	go _ _ _ _ = error "internal"
 	
+	-- relayHelper sends CONNECTDONE when it gets RelayDone.
 	runrelay v = relayHelper runner v >>= \case
 		Left e -> return $ Left e
-		Right exitcode -> runner $
-			net $ relayToPeer (RelayDone exitcode)
+		Right _exitcode -> return $ Right ()
 
-	waitexit v pid = putMVar v . RelayDone =<< waitForProcess pid
+	-- RelayDone is only put once all of the process's output has
+	-- been read and put into the MVar. If it were put as soon as the
+	-- process exited, it could overtake the end of the process's
+	-- output, which would then never be sent to the peer.
+	readthenwaitexit v hout pid = do
+		relayReader v hout
+		putMVar v . RelayDone =<< waitForProcess pid
 
 -- Processes RelayData as it is put into the MVar.
 relayHelper :: RunProto IO -> MVar RelayData -> IO (Either ProtoFailure ExitCode)
